From edaba30e58b8740ced4dd3842773efb346ad096b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:50:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] test(tools): pin the taper tip form before it exists

The pinning tests of #3368. They do not compile until the next commit
adds `Tool::tip_form`, `Tool::tip_diameter` and `crates/tools/src/taper.rs`.

- taper::tests: the tip math of #895, the named refusals, the drawn tip.
- meridian_tests: a sharp taper keeps its profile and meridian bit for
  bit; a flat and a ball tip agree with the profile.
- tool_law: every operation refuses a flat or ball tip by name.
- tool_library, project_roundtrip: the tip round-trips and steps the
  file version only when a tip is not sharp.
- mcp_edit_tool, mcp_deburr: the MCP fields, and the refusal at
  generation after an edit.
- tool_library_editor: the Tip form row.

Refs #3368

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
